# web-console reverse proxy (self-hosted migration off Cloudflare Workers).
#
# Own origin, not shared with caddy-owui or caddy-artifacts: same isolation
# rationale as Caddyfile.artifacts -- a distinct hostname is what keeps this
# app's session cookies out of reach of anything served from HIVE_CHAT_URL or
# ARTIFACTS_DOMAIN, regardless of any in-app defence.
#
# The site address keeps the hostname so the host match still holds, and
# carries an explicit http:// scheme: Caddy turns on automatic HTTPS when a
# site address has no scheme, which redirects plain-HTTP requests back to
# itself and loops forever behind an external TLS terminator (Cloudflare
# Tunnel) -- the same bug already fixed once for Caddyfile.artifacts (PR
# #434, "fix: stop artifacts Caddy site from redirecting to itself forever").
# Naming the scheme disables that redirect without giving up host matching.
#
# X-Forwarded-Proto is stamped explicitly (not trusted from the incoming
# request, since this listener is published on a host port and an inbound
# X-Forwarded-Proto would otherwise be attacker-controlled) so anything
# upstream that derives an absolute URL from request scheme sees the scheme
# users actually arrive on, same pattern as Caddyfile.owui.
http://{$CONSOLE_DOMAIN:-console.localhost} {
  reverse_proxy web-console-prod:3000 {
    header_up X-Forwarded-Proto {$CONSOLE_EXTERNAL_SCHEME:http}
    transport http {
      response_header_timeout 30s
      dial_timeout 5s
    }
  }
}
